{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwZdVxbQaRCEyCfAdsUz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't confirmed that the rule fires. Its status is still \"pending\" because it hadn't run yet when I created it.\n\n**Data:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` is time-based on `timestamp`. Its main fields are:\n- `response`: a string, with a `.keyword` subfield\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `clientip`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-f2ff53e1 Web logs overview\" has five panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (line)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar)\n- Top source countries (table)\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-f2ff53e1-web-logs-overview-9598b322117c.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-f2ff53e1 5xx spike\" (id `47bed22c-65d6-4cd0-9f30-59679e4ae44d`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents match in a 5-minute window. A document matches when `response.keyword` starts with \"5\". I used a prefix match because `response` is stored as a string.\n\nI didn't attach any action connector, so a firing alert will show up in Kibana but won't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1395,"cache_read_input_tokens":19085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1395},"output_tokens":510,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"1091cacf-c6c5-4561-9b84-5f227851f7a8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:35:26.143Z","request_